{#
	The follow-up widget's slot on the dashboard (XIV-81), which since XIV-84 is
	one line: the card is a Live Component, so that narrowing the list does not
	reload the page or put the lens in the URL.

	This file stays rather than being deleted because `DashboardWidget` hands the
	page a *template* and its data (§8.3.1), and a widget whose whole body is a
	component is still a widget. What it must not become is a place where anything
	about follow-ups is decided — that all lives in the component now.

	**`loading="defer"` is XIV-66's only change here**, and it is on this mount
	rather than on the panel. The card is already a Live Component, so deferring it
	is one attribute and one round trip; asking the dashboard to defer the *panel*
	as well would wrap a deferred component inside a deferred component and buy a
	second round trip for nothing. That is why `FollowUpWidget` sets no `defer`
	flag — the widgets whose bodies are plain Twig, which is every widget a module
	can ship, are the ones the dashboard's own mount exists for.

	`loading-template` matches the one the dashboard uses for its deferred panels,
	so the two kinds of waiting look the same to a reader who cannot be expected to
	know there are two.
#}
<twig:DueFollowUps loading="defer" loading-template="dashboard/_loading.html.twig" />
